    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "66144f62_c4984e93",
        "filename": "android/visibility.go",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 141,
      "author": {
        "id": 1373864
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-04-01T19:12:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I suggest introducing a separate //visibility:legacy_public to use as default. That to make migration to more restrictive visibilities easier: At some point the default can change to //visibility:private while a machine refactoring tool adds //visibility:legacy_public to all rules. Then packages can be gradually converted to better explicit visibility settings, and we can tell the difference between public (\u003d intentionally made public) and legacy_public (\u003d no conscious decision on visibility).\n\n(This is under the premise that we aim to move away from public visibility by default, which I think is a good goal.)",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 141,
        "startChar": 61,
        "endLine": 141,
        "endChar": 72
      },
      "revId": "e084826e95eaf4bfac9f604d4e3f400395cd93d9",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e3fc92b0_a2dfd385",
        "filename": "android/visibility.go",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 141,
      "author": {
        "id": 1039338
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-04-02T13:45:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t see the point in adding legacy_public now. It provides no advantage over simply not specifying the visibility property altogether. I definitely agree that defaulting to private is better though. We can easily add legacy_public later once everything has been switched to soong. Doing it any earlier would just make the conversion to soong more difficult.",
      "parentUuid": "66144f62_c4984e93",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 141,
        "startChar": 61,
        "endLine": 141,
        "endChar": 72
      },
      "revId": "e084826e95eaf4bfac9f604d4e3f400395cd93d9",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "53a225d4_b7190def",
        "filename": "android/visibility.go",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 141,
      "author": {
        "id": 1373864
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-04-02T14:11:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The reason to do it now is that it makes the purpose of //visibility:public clear. It can e.g. encourage users to specify //visibility:public explicitly early on, instead of relying on the default.\n\n\u003e Doing it any earlier would just make the conversion to soong more difficult.\n\nIn what way? (Note that I don\u0027t advocate doing the refactoring step at any particular time.)",
      "parentUuid": "e3fc92b0_a2dfd385",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 141,
        "startChar": 61,
        "endLine": 141,
        "endChar": 72
      },
      "revId": "e084826e95eaf4bfac9f604d4e3f400395cd93d9",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "07db052c_f4281979",
        "filename": "android/visibility.go",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 141,
      "author": {
        "id": 1039338
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-04-02T14:39:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t see how adding legacy_public as an allowable rule would encourage users to specify public explicitly anymore than say simply advising them.\n\nSwitching to private by default would make the conversion to soong more difficult because visibility does not apply across makefiles (and there are no plans to make it work). That means makefiles can access targets that are not strictly speaking visible to them. Even if the migration to private does a perfect job and adds all the correct dependencies at the time it is run it is likely that after migration additional dependencies will be added into .mk files that would not actually visible be once it has been migrated which would require updates to files other than the ones being migrated",
      "parentUuid": "53a225d4_b7190def",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 141,
        "startChar": 61,
        "endLine": 141,
        "endChar": 72
      },
      "revId": "e084826e95eaf4bfac9f604d4e3f400395cd93d9",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a02c4a1a_bc44099a",
        "filename": "android/visibility.go",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 141,
      "author": {
        "id": 1373864
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-04-02T17:26:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Right, so I\u0027m not saying //visibility:private should be made the default right now, with the requisite refactoring to keep all packages publicly visible.\n\nWhat I am saying is only to pave the way a bit for it by introducing //visibility:legacy_public and make that default instead of //visibility:public. That\u0027s all - no makefile migration troubles there.\n\n\u003e /.../ anymore than say simply advising them.\n\nThat\u0027s one important purpose with adding legacy_public here, because what place is better to advise people than having it in the code and doc comments? Something like:\n\n  //visibility:public - gives all target access explicitly\n  //visibility:legacy_public - gives all target access by legacy -\n                               the default, please don\u0027t use explicitly",
      "parentUuid": "07db052c_f4281979",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 141,
        "startChar": 61,
        "endLine": 141,
        "endChar": 72
      },
      "revId": "e084826e95eaf4bfac9f604d4e3f400395cd93d9",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
